{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"=== AC3: NEGATIVE mypy PROBE, RUN AND RECORDED. The annotation enforces something. ===\nProbe placed INSIDE the package (src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_cc77_probe.py) so the ONLY\nvariable between the two functions is the import path — same class, same metaclass, same file, one\ncommand (mypy src/rebar, i.e. what make typecheck runs). Removed immediately after measurement.\n\n    from rebar_reconciler._backend import TicketTransport as TT_shim   # sys.path shim\n    from ._backend                import TicketTransport as TT_rel     # relative\n\n    def via_shim(a: TT_shim) -> None:\n        reveal_type(a)\n        a.definitely_not_a_member('x')\n\n    def via_relative(b: TT_rel) -> None:\n        reveal_type(b)\n        b.definitely_not_a_member('x')\n        b.set_entity_property('K-1', 'p', 1)\n\nVERBATIM mypy OUTPUT (ANSI stripped):\n\n    _cc77_probe.py:9:  note: Revealed type is \"Any\"\n    _cc77_probe.py:14: note: Revealed type is \"rebar._engine.rebar_reconciler._backend.TicketTransport\"\n    _cc77_probe.py:15: error: \"TicketTransport\" has no attribute \"definitely_not_a_member\"  [attr-defined]\n\nTHREE THINGS, and note what is ABSENT:\n 1. via_shim line 10 (a.definitely_not_a_member) produced NO OUTPUT AT ALL. Not an error, not a\n    note. The shim-imported annotation is silently Any.\n 2. via_relative line 15 IS an [attr-defined] error — enforcement works, against TODAY'S\n    TicketTransport with _TransportPortMeta still attached. The metaclass is exonerated a third\n    time, now by an independent session.\n 3. via_relative line 16 (set_entity_property, a genuinely declared member) produced NO error. So\n    the annotation DISCRIMINATES; it does not merely make mypy shout at everything. That absence\n    is the load-bearing half — an annotation that errors on everything would be useless.\n\n=== AC2: reveal_type EVIDENCE FOR EVERY TOUCHED MODULE. No annotation silently degraded. ===\nOne port parameter per touched module, probed in a single mypy run, then reverted. 14/14 resolve to\nthe REAL type; ZERO report Any:\n\n    applier.apply                                  -> ...TicketTransport | None\n    apply_inbound._apply_inbound_create            -> ...TicketTransport | None\n    apply_inbound_records._inbound_create_writeback_jira -> ...TicketTransport\n    apply_outbound._apply_outbound_create          -> ...TicketTransport | None\n    batch_dispatch.delete_one                      -> ...TicketTransport\n    binding_store._current_key_by_id               -> ...TicketTransport\n    binding_walk.compute_binding_walk_mutations    -> ...TicketTransport\n    dispatch_apply_phases._update_one_apply_reporter -> ...TicketTransport\n    dispatch_one.create_one                        -> ...TicketTransport\n    fetcher._iter_pages                            -> ...TicketTransport\n    outbound_assignee._bootstrap_account_id_via_user_search -> ...TicketTransport\n    outbound_comments._diff_comments               -> ...TicketTransport | None\n    outbound_differ._safe_get_issue                -> ...TicketTransport\n    typed_dispatch._apply_typed                    -> ...TicketTransport | None\n\n(each '...' is the literal prefix rebar._engine.rebar_reconciler._backend.)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785701840864196001,"uuid":"179f8498-9fd3-4bb1-be00-6d4bc00a4e6f"}